# ReXGlue SDK changes for WWE 2K14 (session57): 3d91313879f7..3313bb8a7ca2 on wwe2k14-local
# Apply in order on upstream rexglue/rexglue-sdk f5337cd (git apply). Commits (first parent):
#  3313bb8 wwe2k14 Session 57 review fixes: AwaitPendingPipeline's 2 s cap is a real deadline (10,000 x 200 us sleeps were 10-20 s on Windows, ~156 s with the window covered); a clear-only resolve no longer resets the skipped-draw count before the copy it is for
#  d9d107c wwe2k14 Session 57 (red patches still reported): gpu_log_skipped_draw_resolves (default on) - a resolve that follows draws skipped while their pipeline was made (placeholders, truth draws and repeats) is logged with what it copies and the widths of the skipped draws' surfaces, the first 40 then every 100th, so a tester's log shows whether skipped draws reach a texture the game keeps
#  e47cf8e wwe2k14 Session 57 (red patches still reported): the screen-wide width for skipping a draw while its pipeline is made is a setting - gpu_native_truth_pipeline_skip_min_pitch (tiles, default 16) and vulkan_pipeline_sync_offscreen_min_pitch (pixels, default 1280); large = never skipped. Defaults unchanged
#  843b019 wwe2k14 Session 57 review fix: the scaled resolve readback binds only this resolve's scaled range (from the storage buffer offset alignment below it) with a shader offset relative to it - the whole buffer from 0 with a 32-bit offset skipped every destination past 4 GiB scaled (the 4K preset's 3x3: guest addresses from ~0x1C71C71D) and bound more than maxStorageBufferRange
#  c1a0e19 wwe2k14 Session 57 (tester bug 4): readback_resolve_override, a readback mode the app sets at run time and GetReadbackResolveMode reads at every resolve (-1 none set, 0 none .. 3 full): the create modes whose GPU-drawn pictures the CPU reads back (a Custom Superstar's render, an arena's menu screenshot) came out as noise with readback off

